Z||000006||frontal lobe||10-19-2001||04:23 PM||||Yeah, I just won an auction for a pontiac cd player off e-bay, and I intentionally waited to bid until the last minute to try to keep the price from being driven up.<P>In my opinion, ebay should have a rule where the auction ends at a certain time, as long as there have been no bids for the last 5 minutes--to be most fair to the seller.  However, they don't do that.  I think some other sites do.||||reg||1
Z||000007||beer_stud_21||10-19-2001||07:03 PM||||Yeah, uBid does that.  I hate it!  its a lot harder to get a good deal!  Because you cant get in at the end before anyone else has a chance to raise their max bid.  If there is more than one person sitting there watching the auction the price can keep going up until someone finally decides they cant afford to go any higher.  Btw:  It's generally thought that ebay prices are a bit high.  I see this quite a bit on computer equipment.<P>-marlin||||reg||1
Z||000008||Ken Wittlief||10-19-2001||08:49 PM||||bidding on ebay is easy, put a low bid in early, just in case nobody else bids, and then about 30 minutes from the end put in a bid for the highest price you are willing to pay. <P> If no body else wants to pay more, you win.<P> If somebody else is willing to pay more than you, then you will loose anyway.<P> ive seen people do some really stupid things on ebay - I saw one auction for a plastic toy lost in space Jupiter 2 go for $176. The name of the manufacture was given in the ad. if you went to <A HREF="http://www.namehere.com" TARGET=_blank>www.namehere.com</A>  you ended up at their website, where you could buy the thing online for $20.<P> Ive also seen instances where some dork really wanted something, like a bootleg CD from some concert (worth maybe $20 max) so to make sure that nobody else outbids them, they put in a bid of $1,000,001.<P> sure enough, some other dork has the same idea, sees the item is now at $20, and bids $1,000,000 at the last second, and guess what? The bid price jumps to a million dollars!<P> Yikes!<P>  You gotta know what stuff is worth, how much you can get it for somewhere else, and how much you want to spend - if you get sucked into 'someone else bid $100 so it must be worth $105...' you are gonna get what you deserve - screwed!||||reg||10
Z||000009||frontal lobe||10-20-2001||12:58 AM||||You can almost ALWAYS do better going to pricewatch.com and looking for computer parts than buying them off e-bay.  Or basically anything new.  People just don't know how to shop around.<P>||||reg||1
